    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Home Bakery WhatsApp Order Assistant\n\n1. Copy the Google Sheet template (tabs **Menu** and **Orders**) and fill your menu.\n2. Edit **Bakery settings**: name, city, hours, notice, delivery, payment.\n3. Connect credentials: WhatsApp Trigger (Meta app ID + secret), WhatsApp (access token + business account ID), OpenAI, Google Sheets.\n4. In **Get_menu** and **Save_order** pick your sheet.\n5. Publish, then message your WhatsApp Business number to test.\n\nFull guide: SETUP-GUIDE.md",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 600
      },
      "id": "8380c20f-84ff-497f-a9ff-31ade4e277d8",
      "name": "Setup (read first)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "WhatsApp also sends delivery/read **status updates** to this trigger. The first check ignores them so the bot never replies to itself. Voice notes and images get a polite *please type* reply.",
        "height": 170,
        "width": 420
      },
      "id": "bd7d4ade-051a-4cca-8e4b-ac8ea137dd95",
      "name": "Why two checks",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        200,
        400
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "The assistant only quotes the menu sheet, confirms the order and total before saving, and hands complaints or custom requests to the owner. If the AI fails, the customer gets a polite fallback instead of silence.",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 380
      },
      "id": "7d75450c-3898-4879-8c91-ee315f47c72f",
      "name": "Agent safety",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
